{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git diff --check\nrg -n 'validate\\\\b' apps/docs/pages\nrg -n 'docs|packed|mkdtemp' rehearsal/test/{runner,reaudit}.test.mjs | head -30\nrg -n '\"'^### 1.3|''^### 1.6'\"' -A26 docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | head -52\"","aggregated_output":"apps/docs/pages/stability.md:34:| Node | Importing `axylo` touches no DOM. `validate()` returns every finding from the input checks, including hints, in every build. For a check you can run with `node check.mjs`, see [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md#validate-in-node-and-in-tests). Charts themselves need a browser. |\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:17:TypeScript 5.4 or later gives you checked field names. The package's declarations refer to DOM types (`HTMLElement`), so a TypeScript project needs the `DOM` library in `lib`, also for code that only calls `validate()` in Node. Plain JavaScript works the same without types.\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:77:**3. Check the values without drawing.** `validate()` runs the chart's input checks in Node or in a test, with the same options as the chart. It returns every finding from those checks, including hints, in every build. In a project with `axylo` installed, save this plain JavaScript as `check.mjs` and run `node check.mjs`.\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:81:To check the monthly visitors chart above in TypeScript, pass its rows and options to `validate()`.\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:84:import { validate } from 'axylo';\napps/docs/pages/getting-started.md:86:const problems = validate('line', { title: 'Monthly visitors', data: rows, x: 'month', y: 'visitors' });\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:59:## validate() in Node and in tests\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:61:`validate(type, options)` runs the same input checks as creating a chart (options, data, view, name) without a DOM. It returns every finding from those checks, including hints, in every build. It takes the same options as the chart type, so it type-checks the same way. Importing `axylo` in Node does not touch the DOM.\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:69:[source: examples/node/validate.ts](../examples/node/validate.ts)\napps/docs/pages/diagnostics.md:75:The documentation tests type-check and run these examples against the packed package. The package's declarations refer to DOM types, so a TypeScript configuration for Node code needs `\"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\"]` (or `skipLibCheck`). Findings that depend on drawing require a browser. `validate()` can check whether you supplied a `title` or `labelledBy`. Checking whether the id exists requires a page.\napps/docs/pages/data.md:174:`validate(type, options)` runs the chart's input checks without a page. It returns every finding from those checks, including hints, in every build. For a check you can run with `node check.mjs`, see [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md#validate-in-node-and-in-tests).\napps/docs/pages/options.md:232:## validate\napps/docs/pages/options.md:234:`validate(type, options)` takes `'line'`, `'area'`, `'bar'`, `'scatter'` or `'donut'` and that type's options. It runs the chart's input checks without a DOM and returns every finding in a `Diagnostic[]`, including hints, in every build. Checks for contrast, sizes, label fitting, formatters and matching a `labelledBy` id need a page. For a check you can run with `node check.mjs`, see [Diagnostics](diagnostics.md#validate-in-node-and-in-tests).\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:3:import { cp, mkdir, mkdtemp, open, readFile, rm, symlink, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:36:beforeEach(async () => { scratch = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'axylo-reaudit-test-')); });\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:70:it('ignores paths in patterns, option values, inline programs, heredocs and command output', async () => {\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:72:    \"rg -n --glob '/etc/hostname' '/etc/hostname' docs/options.html\",\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:73:    \"sed -e 's:/etc/hostname::g' docs/index.html\",\nrehearsal/test/reaudit.test.mjs:91:      { type: 'tool_use', name: 'Glob', input: { path: 'docs', pattern: '**/*.html' } },\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:1:import { access, chmod, copyFile, cp, lstat, mkdir, mkdtemp, open, readFile, readdir, readlink, rm, stat, symlink, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:36:beforeEach(async () => { scratch = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'axylo-rehearsal-test-')); });\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:49:it('audits complete Codex and Claude logs while allowing the copied docs and system tools', async () => {\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:50:  const codex = codexLog(command(\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/getting-started.html; node ./chart.js'\", scratch),\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:219:  expect(workspaceEntries).toBe('PROMPT.md data.json docs node_modules package.json');\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:278:  expect((await readdir(first.workspace)).sort()).toEqual(['PROMPT.md', 'data.json', 'docs', 'node_modules', 'package.json']);\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:279:  for (const path of ['docs', 'docs/getting-started.html', 'node_modules', 'node_modules/axylo/dist/axylo.js', 'data.json']) {\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:282:  await access(join(first.workspace, 'docs/source/apps/docs/examples/daily-sessions.ts.html'));\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:283:  await expect(access(join(first.workspace, 'docs/source/packages'))).rejects.toHaveProperty('code', 'ENOENT');\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:298:it('bundles the packed browser entry and reports a Chrome launch failure', async () => {\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:321:  const other = await mkdtemp(join(scratch, 'axylo-rehearsal-'));\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:398:      docs: expect.stringMatching(/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/), grader: expect.stringMatching(/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/) },\nrehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs:508:    hashes: { docs: 'docs', grader: 'grader', package: 'package' }, cli: { version: cell.agent }, browserVersion: 'fixture Chrome',\n63:### 1.3 Fields\n64-\n65-A field is a key of the row, or an object when it needs more. The key is checked against the row type by role: a value axis accepts number fields; text fields are accepted there only with `parse: 'number'`.\n66-\n67-```ts\n68-line(el, {\n69-  data: samples,\n70-  x: { field: 'ts', type: 'time', timeZone: 'UTC' },\n71-  y: { field: 'sessions', label: 'Sessions', unit: 'sessions', tickFormat: { notation: 'compact' } },\n72-});\n73-\n74-// counts that a database driver returns as strings\n75-bar(el, { data: pgRows, x: 'day', y: { field: 'count', parse: 'number', missing: 'zero' } });\n76-```\n77-\n78-| Option | Meaning |\n79-|---|---|\n80-| `field` | Key of the row. |\n81-| `label`, `unit` | Axis title; name and unit in tooltip, table and announcements. |\n82-| `type` (x) | `'date'`, `'time'`, `'number'`, `'category'`. Inferred when omitted, except that a number is never inferred to be an instant (F4). |\n83-| `timeZone` (x) | For instants: `'local'` (default), `'UTC'`, or an IANA zone. |\n84-| `format`, `tickFormat` | Readouts and ticks are formatted separately (F6). |\n85-| `scale` (value) | `'percent'` (0–100) or `'ratio'` (0–1). Declared, never inferred (F7). |\n86-| `missing` (value) | `'gap'` (default) or `'zero'` (F2). |\n87-| `parse` (value) | `'number'`, for a text field holding numbers (AX104, AX106). |\n88-| `domain` | Author bounds. Widened to zero on bar and area (F1). |\n89-\n--\n130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\n131-\n132-The registry, with each code's level and outcome, is in the spec (section 3.5). Example for the Phase 1 combined dirty fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`):\n133-\n134-```\n135-[axylo AX103] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" has 1 value that is not a finite number (NaN at row 3). Shown as a gap.\n136-  Check the calculation that produced it, or send null for \"no data\".\n137-[axylo AX106] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" mixes numbers with 1 string (\"40\" at row 4). The string is not plotted.\n138-  Convert it to a number where the data is produced.\n139-[axylo AX102] \"Dirty input\": y field \"value\" is absent in 1 row (row 5). Shown as a gap.\n140-  Send null if the value is known to be missing.\n141-```\n142-\n143-The reader of that chart sees \"Values not shown: 3. See table.\" (F12).\n144-\n145-`validate(type, options)` runs the same normalization without a DOM and returns the diagnostics, so a server, a test or a coding agent can check a chart before rendering it.\n146-\n147-Development and production flavours are selected through package `exports` conditions. The script-tag distribution ships `axylo.js` (development) and `axylo.min.js` (production). Errors and warnings print once per code per page in both; hints only in development.\n148-\n149-### 1.7 React adapter (not in 1.0)\n150-\n151-Removed from the first release by the owner on 2026-11-18: 1.0 is plain TypeScript, and adapters for React, Vue, Svelte and others follow later. The adapter described below was built, reviewed twice and fixed; its last state is `packages/react` at commit dac5664. The section is kept as the design to return to.\n152-\n153-```tsx\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
